"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3036,"**
Narrated to us Al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman who said: Al-Shafi'i said: Malik informed us.

Also narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la who said: Ibn Wahb informed us that Malik informed him, from Ibn Shihab, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas (RA) that he said:

Al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas (RA) was riding behind the Prophet (ﷺ). A woman from Khath'am came to ask him a question. Al-Fadl began looking at her, and she began looking at him. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned Al-Fadl's face to the other side. She said: ""O Messenger of Allah, indeed Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has reached my father, an elderly man who is unable to ride steadily. May I perform Hajj on his behalf?""

He (ﷺ) said: ""Yes.""

This was during the Farewell Pilgrimage.

---"
